                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4bea71a2-6bdf-31a6-aeaf-2582d4dff97c",
                                        "entry_id": "de86c958-7028-35be-a02d-50a1c0c5c534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To mathematically calculate a numeric result."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "990b6ae3-6f16-3b68-acbe-e5f30e63258c",
                                        "entry_id": "de86c958-7028-35be-a02d-50a1c0c5c534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To record something by making marks."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b5319b3-0420-433e-adb0-b6052ae0d375",
                                                "sense_id": "990b6ae3-6f16-3b68-acbe-e5f30e63258c",
                                                "text": "The counter tallied the languages people were conversing in while walking along a set route that wove back and forth through the chairs and tables."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8825abf4-3b42-3013-ba31-a916ad652844",
                                        "entry_id": "de86c958-7028-35be-a02d-50a1c0c5c534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To make things correspond or agree with each other."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "00f370cf-b337-44ca-96e2-254d525926b0",
                                                "sense_id": "8825abf4-3b42-3013-ba31-a916ad652844",
                                                "text": "I am sorry to find they are not so well tallied to the present juncture as I could wish."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "34e03ef1-2101-3f01-be40-7ddfcf28948a",
                                        "entry_id": "de86c958-7028-35be-a02d-50a1c0c5c534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To keep score."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5945226b-199e-335e-a799-416a29addbd8",
                                        "entry_id": "de86c958-7028-35be-a02d-50a1c0c5c534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To correspond or agree."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2eb85301-bbbe-449e-b45d-143a2f2e9fcd",
                                                "sense_id": "5945226b-199e-335e-a799-416a29addbd8",
                                                "text": "In some I found pieces of tiles that exactly tallied with the channel, and in others a little wall of bricks"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3576f0b6-7bc0-4e9d-83fe-23d22ebada42",
                                                "sense_id": "5945226b-199e-335e-a799-416a29addbd8",
                                                "text": "Your idea, my dear lord, of the abusive paragraph on you being conceived at Paris, and transmitted hither, tallies exactly with mine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a604b951-1371-4a2f-b6f3-2612fed9648d",
                                                "sense_id": "5945226b-199e-335e-a799-416a29addbd8",
                                                "text": "This credulity will not be challenged here; yet it may be remarked that, assuming the unlimited and unvarying benevolence of the powerful planners, our analysis shows that it may be impossible for them ever to find out whether the results of their measures tally with their good intentions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ae6bf75f-3c59-447e-a1b8-ffe443b959b3",
                                                "sense_id": "5945226b-199e-335e-a799-416a29addbd8",
                                                "text": "However, one abiding weakness with such data collection is that people’s beliefs about their speech habits may not necessarily tally with reality."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f58e3e4-9e44-3a02-a36d-a84fd89f70d8",
                                        "entry_id": "de86c958-7028-35be-a02d-50a1c0c5c534",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To check off, as parcels of freight going inboard or outboard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8e409ac9-08e5-4eed-bb31-fdc4ee913bc0",
                                                "sense_id": "1f58e3e4-9e44-3a02-a36d-a84fd89f70d8",
                                                "text": "I loaded a cargo of potatoes in Dublin, for Bangor and Caernarvon, all in bags, for three different parties—viz. 13 tons delivered at Bangor, which was tallied in and out; remainder to Caernarvon, and was not tallied in, but tallied out."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
